# ============================================================================
# TRAME EDGE ROUTES (trame-routes.caddy), imported inside a site block
# ============================================================================
#
# PURPOSE:
# --------
# One routing table for both edge variants (`Caddyfile`: public HTTPS;
# `Caddyfile.tunnel`: plain HTTP behind Cloudflare Tunnel), so the two cannot
# drift apart.
#
# INVARIANTS & SAFETY BOUNDARIES:
# -------------------------------
#   1. `Same-Origin Silo Downloads`:
#      - With the Silo variant, `S3_PUBLIC_ENDPOINT` equals
#        `TRAME_PUBLIC_ORIGIN`, so presigned URLs look like
#        `{origin}/{S3_BUCKET}/{key}?X-Amz-...`. Only read methods on that
#        bucket path reach Silo; writes stay on the internal network.
#      - Caddy passes the client `Host` through unchanged: SigV4 signs the
#        public host, so rewriting it would break every signature.
#      - With R2 (or no object store) nothing listens on `silo:9000` and the
#        path answers `502`; it is otherwise unused.
#   2. `No Second Compression Pass`:
#      - There is deliberately no `encode` directive. `trame-server` already
#        negotiates gzip/br/zstd and skips images and fonts, and WebSocket
#        frames are deflated by the `trame.v1+deflate` subprotocol. Caddy
#        relays bodies and `Content-Encoding` untouched.
#   3. `Long-Lived WebSockets`:
#      - Caddy proxies `Upgrade` requests and the `Sec-WebSocket-Protocol`
#        header as-is. Upgraded streams have no read or idle timeout; the
#        server's 20 s ping heartbeat keeps intermediaries (Cloudflare drops
#        idle sockets after 100 s) from closing them.
#      - `stream_close_delay` keeps open sockets alive for 5 minutes across a
#        `caddy reload` instead of cutting every table at once.
# ============================================================================

@silo_download {
	path /{$S3_BUCKET:trame-assets}/*
	method GET HEAD OPTIONS
}

handle @silo_download {
	reverse_proxy silo:9000
}

handle {
	reverse_proxy trame-server:8080 {
		stream_close_delay 5m
	}
}
